  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 1250 PM MDT Tue Aug 18 2026\n\nAdditional moisture will spread westward into the state by Thursday \nas the mid-level ridge shifts northeast toward the Four Corners and \neventually northern New Mexico. This pattern should lead to an \nincrease in shower and thunderstorm coverage Thursday and Friday, \nwith scattered to numerous storms possible across much of the \narea. Instability and shear may again support a few strong to \nsevere storms, mainly across northeastern New Mexico. Increasing \nsoil moisture and repeated rainfall with elevate the flash \nflooding threat as well. Temperatures will remain hot with \nportions of the Rio Grande Valley and eastern plains returning to \nthe low 100s. \n\nBy the weekend, the ridge is expected to strengthen and settle \nnear the eastern New Mexico/Texas Panhandle border, while drier \nair begins filtering into southern New Mexico from the southeast.\nThis should gradually reduce storm coverage, although isolated to\nscattered convection will remain possible along the central \nmountain chain and westward. Temperatures will remain above \naverage through early next week, with triple digit highs \npersisting across the lower Rio Grande Valley and eastern plains.",
